====================================================================================================
 READING IT
====================================================================================================
  'oracle' is a FEASIBILITY GATE. If it is not near 100% at a given
  size, nothing at that size is recoverable for reasons unrelated to
  search, and the search/random cells there say nothing.


  Compare the search-to-random gap ACROSS sizes, not within one.
  Growing gap  -> real selection power, concentrated where
                  enumeration is infeasible (the method's claim).
  Flat/shrinking -> no selection power that survives scale; at small
                  sizes enumerate instead.
